From: j7 smp
Subject: j7prime: start all eight Cortex-A53 cores (cpus=8)

The A5XELTE build (Galaxy J7 Prime / A5 2016) was hard-capped at one CPU: SWEET_SMP_MAX_CPUS 1
and SweetCPU::start() panicking unless num_cpus == 1. The PSCI CPU_ON + GICv2 SGI bring-up that
already runs 8/8 cores on the S7 (0208, 0218, 0219) is guarded by HEROLTE only because that board
was the first to need it. Share it through A5XELTE_SMP.

Exynos7870 order: logical 0..3 = MPIDR 0..3 (boot cluster), 4..7 = MPIDR 0x100..0x103. The ADT
must describe one XNU cluster (cluster-id/die-cluster-id 0, as mkadt_herolte.py does): the old
two-cluster attempt (0115) panicked CPU0 on an owned ticket lock while registering cluster 2.
Select the core count with the cpus=N boot-arg (cpus=4 = boot cluster only).

diff --git a/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/A5XELTE.h b/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/A5XELTE.h
--- a/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/A5XELTE.h
+++ b/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/A5XELTE.h
@@ -8,6 +8,8 @@
 #define A5XELTE                       1
 /* Reuse donor's SoC-neutral early services until their guards are renamed. */
 #define SWEET                         1
+/* Secondary-CPU bring-up (PSCI CPU_ON + GICv2 SGIs) shared by HEROLTE and the 4+4 A53 boards. */
+#define A5XELTE_SMP                   1
 
 /* Firmware scanout buffer and the earliest XNU marker (physical). */
 #if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_HEROLTE)
@@ -27,7 +29,8 @@
 /* S-Boot starts on the Cortex-A53 "Apollo" cluster, Aff1 = 1. */
 #define A5XELTE_BOOT_MPIDR            0x100
 #else
-#define SWEET_SMP_MAX_CPUS            1
+/* Exynos7870/7580: logical 0..3 = MPIDR 0..3 (boot cluster), 4..7 = MPIDR 0x100..0x103. */
+#define SWEET_SMP_MAX_CPUS            8
 #define A5XELTE_FB_PA                 0x67000000
 #define A5XELTE_FB_WIDTH              1080
 #define A5XELTE_FB_HEIGHT             1920
